#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/database_types_list.rst:6
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduktion"

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/database_types_list.rst:8
msgid ""
"The purpose of the Database Type Map is to simplify the process of creating "
"installations for multiple database systems. Instead of writing specific "
"installation instructions for each individual database system, you can "
"create a single set of instructions and use the Database Type Map to modify "
"any supported database system with just one command. This makes it easier "
"and more efficient to work with multiple database systems, as you don't need"
" to write and maintain separate instructions for each one."
msgstr ""
"Formålet med Database Type Map er at forenkle processen med at oprette "
"installationer til flere databasesystemer. I stedet for at skrive specifikke"
" installationsinstruktioner til hvert enkelt databasesystem kan du oprette "
"ét enkelt sæt instruktioner og bruge Database Type Map til at ændre ethvert "
"understøttet databasesystem med blot én kommando. Dette gør det nemmere og "
"mere effektivt at arbejde med flere databasesystemer, da du ikke behøver at "
"skrive og vedligeholde separate instruktioner til hvert af dem."

#: ../../devdocs-source-copy/extensions/database_types_list.rst:16
msgid ""
"With some commands you may enter the `Zerofill "
"<https://www.tutorialspoint.com/what-is-the-benefit-of-zerofill-in-mysql>`_,"
" example ``INT:11``, if the field is a numeric one. With some you may enter "
"the length of the field, example ``VARCHAR:255``, which will make a "
"varchar(255) column in MySQL. In all of the fields supporting this, they "
"will have a colon followed by ``%d`` meaning any number may fill the space "
"of the ``%d``."
msgstr ""
"Med nogle kommandoer kan du angive `Zerofill "
"<https://www.tutorialspoint.com/what-is-the-benefit-of-zerofill-in-mysql>`_,"
" f.eks. ``INT:11``, hvis feltet er numerisk. Med nogle kan du angive feltets"
" længde, f.eks. ``VARCHAR:255``, hvilket vil give en varchar(255)-kolonne i "
"MySQL. I alle de felter, der understøtter dette, vil de have et kolon "
"efterfulgt af ``%d``, hvilket betyder, at et hvilket som helst tal kan "
"udfylde pladsen for ``%d``."

